WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.403 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:07.040
-I want to start by saying,
if you can sense a vibe...

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.975
Are you [bleep] kidding me?

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:10.643
[ Laughter ]

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:13.680
Wally and Scollins
come in chatting it up.

00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:19.052
During "Corrections."

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:25.592
Is nothing sacred
in this place?

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:27.494
Was that one of
the guild requests?

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:30.697
"I wanna be able to talk
during 'Corrections.'"

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:32.665
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:43.309
Well.

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:49.349
I apologize
that you had to see that.

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:51.684
But if you don't shame them
in the moment,

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.553
they don't learn their lesson.

00:00:58.524 --> 00:01:01.528
I was gonna open
by explaining...

00:01:01.528 --> 00:01:03.530
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.731 --> 00:01:08.101
..."Corrections" is gonna be
a little looser.

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:10.103
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:13.272
And I realize I betrayed that
right off the bat.

00:01:13.272 --> 00:01:14.607
But one of the reasons

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:19.445
"Corrections" is gonna have
a different vibe now

00:01:19.445 --> 00:01:23.783
is that it is no longer
Emmy-nominated.

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:25.652
For two years,
it was Emmy-nominated.

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:29.922
And then during the strike,
it was un-nominated,

00:01:29.922 --> 00:01:32.091
I think is the term they use.

00:01:32.091 --> 00:01:35.295
If you don't get nominated, you
just don't find out anything.

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:37.296
If you were nominated
and then you're not,

00:01:37.296 --> 00:01:39.966
they call you

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:42.034
and they request
that you stop

00:01:42.034 --> 00:01:45.471
describing the work
as Emmy-nominated.

00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:48.507
But, you know,
the thing about that is

00:01:48.507 --> 00:01:50.342
I...

00:01:50.342 --> 00:01:52.111
I feel as though
a burden has been lifted,

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:54.447
because I will admit
that it went to my head

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:56.249
and I did start chasing
the Emmy gold.

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:58.318
I didn't start
doing the corrections

00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:00.453
I thought were important to do.
I started doing the corrections

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:03.623
that I thought the voters
would want me to do.

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:05.691
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.691 --> 00:02:09.896
And now I can just go back
to the integrity of the work,

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:13.365
which is what
this has always been.

00:02:13.365 --> 00:02:14.733
Because I think,
when done right,

00:02:14.733 --> 00:02:18.570
this is unlike anything
you watch on...

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:20.573
I don't know, your phone?

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:22.575
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:25.945
Propped against the toaster
while you're drinking coffee.

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:32.184
So, with that relief that
this is no longer a show

00:02:32.184 --> 00:02:34.888
that is Emmy-nominated,
came enthusiasm as I jumped

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:38.858
into the comments
of our viewers today.

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:43.829
And the first comment
I read said,

00:02:43.829 --> 00:02:46.065
"I was surprised
he hasn't been doing these.

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:48.768
I thought he could do
'Corrections' during the strike

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:50.436
because the only thing
the writers provide

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:52.772
is forced laughter."

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:55.641
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.641 --> 00:02:58.244
I don't need writers

00:02:58.244 --> 00:02:59.912
to provide forced laughter.

00:02:59.912 --> 00:03:01.581
I got Buck.

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:03.683
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:07.753
And that's not forced laughter.

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:09.422
Now, don't get me wrong.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:12.792
I'm sure when he was a kid,
somebody forced him to laugh...

00:03:15.294 --> 00:03:16.629
...and now he can't stop.

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:18.130
I mean, I think
we're dealing with

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:20.700
some sort of deep-seated trauma

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.536
that every one of these works.

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:27.073
"Bucky, come over to your mama.
I'm funny, aren't I, Bucky?"

00:03:27.073 --> 00:03:28.407
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.407 --> 00:03:30.376
"Oh, Bucky, I don't know
what I'd do

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:33.679
if my baby didn't think
I was funny.

00:03:33.679 --> 00:03:35.515
Bucky."

00:03:35.515 --> 00:03:37.750
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.754
Is it worth...

00:03:42.754 --> 00:03:44.390
Here's a question we had.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:45.558
When we did our first show
on Monday,

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:46.992
was it worth doing
"A Closer Look"

00:03:46.992 --> 00:03:48.294
that covered
the last five months?

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:51.563
Is it worth...
Same question.

00:03:51.563 --> 00:03:53.799
Is it worth doing
a "Corrections"

00:03:53.799 --> 00:03:56.435
and going back and correcting
the last week of shows

00:03:56.435 --> 00:03:59.772
we did five months ago
that went uncorrected.

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:01.506
Because people won't even
remember the errors

00:04:01.506 --> 00:04:02.842
from five months ago.

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:04.177
It is worth it,
because I remember.

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:06.479
I have a photographic memory
of this show.

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:10.416
I have basically
spent five months

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:13.252
eating myself up inside
due to the mistakes

00:04:13.252 --> 00:04:14.687
I made
that I had not addressed.

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:17.557
So I am going to start
by addressing mistakes

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:19.825
from five years ago
that I still remember.

00:04:19.825 --> 00:04:22.027
Five months ago.
Excuse me.

00:04:22.027 --> 00:04:24.197
Here's the first one.

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:27.600
The call with Aunt Joan
said "slide to answer."

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.535
That means the call
hadn't been answered yet.

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:30.970
It was still
an incoming call.

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:32.572
The [bleep]?

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:34.540
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:38.744
The sun doesn't go
behind the moon.

00:04:38.744 --> 00:04:41.848
The moon goes
in front of the sun.

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:44.650
The easiest way to remember
that is I don't sit

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:46.985
behind a standing Shoemaker
at a meeting.

00:04:46.985 --> 00:04:50.323
I sit, and then he comes
and stands in front of me.

00:04:50.323 --> 00:04:52.558
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:54.861
Apologies, by the way,
to Shoemaker's neighbors.

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:57.196
Can't imagine you had
a good five months.

00:04:57.196 --> 00:04:59.265
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.403 --> 00:05:06.906
Our last episode,
we made a lot of fun

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:11.010
about Tucker Carlson
getting fired from Fox News.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:13.713
Joke's on us.
Guy landed on his feet.

00:05:15.682 --> 00:05:19.052
Oh, another guy we made fun of
our last show, Ron DeSantis.

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:20.552
We did an impression of him

00:05:20.552 --> 00:05:23.222
eating pudding
with three fingers.

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:24.556
And a jackal asked,

00:05:24.556 --> 00:05:27.727
"Why are you so sure
the three figures --

00:05:27.727 --> 00:05:30.763
the three fingers
are contiguous?"

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:32.364
And I think,
knowing Ron DeSantis

00:05:32.364 --> 00:05:34.533
and how weird he is,

00:05:34.533 --> 00:05:37.103
I'm pretty confident
it might be like...

00:05:39.638 --> 00:05:41.307
...this.

00:05:41.307 --> 00:05:43.710
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.646 --> 00:05:50.249
I don't think he's gonna
be president, guys.

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:51.751
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.751 --> 00:05:53.085
Before the break,
we were talking about

00:05:53.085 --> 00:05:55.855
the Stevie Nicks song
"White Winged Dove."

00:05:55.855 --> 00:05:58.124
A lot of you told me the name
of the song is "Edge of 17."

00:05:58.124 --> 00:06:01.094
And not to give a correction
to a legend like Stevie Nicks,

00:06:01.094 --> 00:06:03.229
but just [bleep] change it.

00:06:03.229 --> 00:06:05.431
Don't "Baba O'Riley"
your songs.

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:08.333
Make it be the title
people want it to be.

00:06:08.333 --> 00:06:10.436
You know, when you do that,
that just means some [bleep]

00:06:10.436 --> 00:06:12.371
at a karaoke night
gets to run the computer

00:06:12.371 --> 00:06:13.539
and people go up
and they're like,

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:15.108
"I would love to do
'White Winged Dove.'"

00:06:15.108 --> 00:06:18.611
He's like, "I can't find it.

00:06:18.611 --> 00:06:20.513
I don't think it's a song."

00:06:22.615 --> 00:06:25.385
Someone said the sound
Stevie Nicks makes in that song

00:06:25.385 --> 00:06:26.885
sounds more like an owl
than a dove.

00:06:26.885 --> 00:06:28.087
And I thought,
Oh, I know what I'll do.

00:06:28.087 --> 00:06:29.956
I'll say,
"Oh, let's take a listen,"

00:06:29.956 --> 00:06:32.925
and I'd play a clip
from that song.

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:34.460
And then we'd put in,
you know,

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:37.229
an actual owl's hoots
over the doves.

00:06:37.229 --> 00:06:39.098
But I can't do that.
The reason we didn't do that

00:06:39.098 --> 00:06:43.602
is when you use a song,
due to music licensing,

00:06:43.602 --> 00:06:44.937
it can't be on YouTube.

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:46.272
And I'm not complaining.

00:06:46.272 --> 00:06:48.174
That's the rule
for everything.

00:06:48.174 --> 00:06:50.008
You know, we put a song
in "Corrections,"

00:06:50.008 --> 00:06:51.510
it comes off YouTube.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:53.713
Same is true
of "Carpool Karaoke."

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:56.816
[ Laughter ]

00:07:03.121 --> 00:07:04.456
By the way,
I don't want to...

00:07:04.456 --> 00:07:07.460
I already regret being critical
of Stevie Nicks.

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:10.362
That is not someone
you want to run afoul of.

00:07:10.362 --> 00:07:14.467
You ever listen to the lyrics
of "Silver Springs"?

00:07:14.467 --> 00:07:16.635
Ask Lindsey Buckingham.

00:07:16.635 --> 00:07:18.204
Because if you run afoul
of Stevie Nicks,

00:07:18.204 --> 00:07:20.206
you wake up in the morning...

00:07:20.206 --> 00:07:22.608
just a scarf on your pillow.

00:07:26.411 --> 00:07:29.849
Oh, people say, "What's in your
drink, and do you finish it?"

00:07:29.849 --> 00:07:33.185
It is a negroni,
and I do finish it.

00:07:33.185 --> 00:07:34.753
Not during "Corrections."

00:07:34.753 --> 00:07:37.690
I stay here the whole weekend,

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:38.924
in the dark,

00:07:38.924 --> 00:07:40.693
just slowly sipping it,
and I try to finish

00:07:40.693 --> 00:07:43.429
right before
Monday's "Closer Look."

00:07:45.564 --> 00:07:49.335
We said Donald Trump
has been indicted three times,

00:07:49.335 --> 00:07:51.937
which was one more
than the Unabomber.

00:07:51.937 --> 00:07:54.206
And then I said,
"Who, as the Una implies,

00:07:54.206 --> 00:07:55.408
just had the one."

00:07:55.408 --> 00:07:57.843
I put that in.
Really liked it.

00:07:57.843 --> 00:08:01.013
Nary a laugh from the audience.

00:08:01.013 --> 00:08:03.549
And then a bunch of you
said the Una in Unabomber

00:08:03.549 --> 00:08:04.917
was for his bombing targets.

00:08:04.917 --> 00:08:07.853
The U-N was for universities,
the A was for airlines.

00:08:07.853 --> 00:08:11.990
A Uni-bomber would be someone
who bombs only once.

00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:14.827
Like me when I told
the Unabomber joke.

00:08:14.827 --> 00:08:16.995
[ Laughter ]

00:08:16.995 --> 00:08:21.133
And thanks to our eagle-eyed
viewer who sent in all that

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:23.636
Unabomber information,
Conner O'Malley.

00:08:23.636 --> 00:08:25.671
[ Laughter ]

00:08:29.475 --> 00:08:31.777
We said Trump looked like
a Klingon general in court

00:08:31.777 --> 00:08:33.479
and then showed a picture
of Worf

00:08:33.479 --> 00:08:36.082
from "Star Trek:
The Next Generation."

00:08:36.082 --> 00:08:39.385
He was a lieutenant,
I was told by a bunch of people.

00:08:39.385 --> 00:08:42.621
That was a bad choice
for a Klingon general.

00:08:42.621 --> 00:08:44.724
General Martok
would have worked.

00:08:46.959 --> 00:08:50.796
I don't like the expression
"you people,"

00:08:50.796 --> 00:08:53.299
because it usually implies
the speaker has

00:08:53.299 --> 00:08:56.769
some pretty bad prejudices.

00:08:56.769 --> 00:08:58.270
With that said,
I'd just like to say

00:08:58.270 --> 00:08:59.672
to the Star Trek fans
out there --

00:08:59.672 --> 00:09:01.173
you people.

00:09:01.173 --> 00:09:02.808
[ Laughter ]

00:09:04.309 --> 00:09:05.711
We also said you could
never be a general

00:09:05.711 --> 00:09:08.714
because the Starfleet uses
the ranks of the Navy.

00:09:08.714 --> 00:09:11.918
Because I guess in the future,
space is water.

00:09:14.286 --> 00:09:16.389
Taco Bell has had breakfast
since 2014.

00:09:16.389 --> 00:09:18.724
They just added
the breakfast taco.

00:09:18.724 --> 00:09:20.526
What's going on over there?

00:09:20.526 --> 00:09:22.928
[ Laughter ]

00:09:22.928 --> 00:09:25.298
Got to be stoned
to work there, too?

00:09:30.136 --> 00:09:33.772
Aaron Rodgers did not,
as I said yesterday,

00:09:33.772 --> 00:09:36.474
tear his ACL.

00:09:36.474 --> 00:09:39.645
He tore his Achilles.

00:09:39.645 --> 00:09:42.148
That's the last time
I do my own research.

00:09:42.148 --> 00:09:44.317
[ Laughter ]

00:09:47.519 --> 00:09:49.855
I said Laphonza Butler
is the first

00:09:49.855 --> 00:09:51.457
Black lesbian woman
in the Senate.

00:09:51.457 --> 00:09:54.126
I was told lesbian
and woman are redundant.

00:09:54.126 --> 00:09:55.827
And then I decided to say
that information

00:09:55.827 --> 00:09:58.097
as flatly as possible
and move on.

00:10:05.303 --> 00:10:09.908
I don't love giving corrections
to my colleagues,

00:10:09.908 --> 00:10:13.211
but oftentimes they don't have
a way to give them.

00:10:13.211 --> 00:10:16.415
We showed a clip
of Sean Hannity,

00:10:16.415 --> 00:10:18.985
and it's about how Trump

00:10:18.985 --> 00:10:20.386 line:0%
was gonna be
the next House speaker.

00:10:20.386 --> 00:10:25.123 line:0%
And instead of former,
they said "fromer."

00:10:25.123 --> 00:10:26.458 line:0%
Which I think
is maybe how they...

00:10:26.458 --> 00:10:28.760 line:0%
Like, if Trump calls up angrily
and he's like,

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:31.797 line:0%
"I'm not the former president,"
they're like, "Fromer."

00:10:38.037 --> 00:10:41.040
A lot of people said that's not
where their ears would be.

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:43.275
[ Laughter ]

00:10:51.149 --> 00:10:52.518
Ah.

00:10:54.886 --> 00:10:58.123
We showed Trump Tower.

00:10:58.123 --> 00:11:00.459
We made it look like
"The Honeymooners."

00:11:00.459 --> 00:11:02.127
And someone said,

00:11:02.127 --> 00:11:03.561
"Oh, my God, you should do
'Honeymooners.'"

00:11:03.561 --> 00:11:05.831
This is like not a correction.
This is like a pitch.

00:11:05.831 --> 00:11:06.965
Like, "You should do a bit

00:11:06.965 --> 00:11:08.901
where Trump's like,
'To the moon, Mel.'"

00:11:08.901 --> 00:11:10.302
But, like, you have
to remember, like,

00:11:10.302 --> 00:11:13.639
Trump would not have any power
in that relationship.

00:11:13.639 --> 00:11:15.474
If Trump was like Ralph Kramden,
he'd be like,

00:11:15.474 --> 00:11:16.642
"To the moon, Mel."

00:11:16.642 --> 00:11:17.977
She'd be like,
"I'll tell them everything,"

00:11:17.977 --> 00:11:20.513
And he'd be like,
"Look who's back from the moon."

00:11:23.382 --> 00:11:25.383
I forgot we had a P.O. Box,

00:11:25.383 --> 00:11:29.187
so it was fun to come in
and see some stuff.

00:11:29.187 --> 00:11:32.458
I've got...
I got top three.

00:11:32.458 --> 00:11:35.594
Someone said, you know,

00:11:35.594 --> 00:11:38.263
"Sorry you didn't get nominated
for an Emmy."

00:11:38.263 --> 00:11:40.933
But again, don't be sorry.
It's a relief.

00:11:40.933 --> 00:11:42.935
[ Laughter ]

00:11:42.935 --> 00:11:47.605
Imagine how mad I'd be
if this was Emmy-nominated

00:11:47.605 --> 00:11:50.609
and [bleep] Scollins and Wally
are just walking in...

00:11:50.609 --> 00:11:53.278
[ Laughter ]

00:11:53.278 --> 00:11:54.913
You guys remember,
this all started with Legos.

00:11:54.913 --> 00:11:57.248
Somebody made a Lego me,
and they...

00:11:57.248 --> 00:11:59.584
That's a little Emmy.

00:11:59.584 --> 00:12:01.754
I would've put it in the hand,
but it doesn't fit in the hand,

00:12:01.754 --> 00:12:03.756
which I feel like
might be the joke.

00:12:03.756 --> 00:12:05.491
[ Laughter ]

00:12:11.196 --> 00:12:16.135 line:0%
And that is a Mac Tonight
with a jackal in his pocket.

00:12:16.135 --> 00:12:18.470 line:0%
And I don't know
if you can see this.

00:12:18.470 --> 00:12:21.139 line:0%
I couldn't quite understand
what they're doing here.

00:12:21.139 --> 00:12:23.709 line:0%
It says -- There's a picture
of a Pizza Hatz

00:12:23.709 --> 00:12:25.544 line:0%
that I guess goes on it,
but it's hard to read.

00:12:25.544 --> 00:12:28.347
But it says,

00:12:28.347 --> 00:12:32.217
"Accessories sold separately."

00:12:32.217 --> 00:12:33.718
So they made me a present

00:12:33.718 --> 00:12:36.388
and showed me a picture
of another thing they made,

00:12:36.388 --> 00:12:38.390
and I guess I gotta buy it.

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:40.159
[ Laughter ]

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:45.664
But then someone took the cake.

00:12:45.664 --> 00:12:48.167
I mean, they said...
Somebody made this and said,

00:12:48.167 --> 00:12:50.235
"I'm willing
to give you the patent" --

00:12:50.235 --> 00:12:53.405
I mean, they wanted
to split the money.

00:12:53.405 --> 00:12:55.641
Sell it at the NBC Store.

00:12:55.641 --> 00:12:59.912
And it's for the Seth fans
who are also jackal fans.

00:13:02.147 --> 00:13:04.650
[ Laughter ]

00:13:09.654 --> 00:13:12.490
[ Laughter continues ]

00:13:12.490 --> 00:13:15.361
I mean, it's the most
haunting thing I've ever seen.

00:13:18.063 --> 00:13:19.698
And you know, now...

00:13:23.803 --> 00:13:26.771
Now is when I weigh something,
right?

00:13:26.771 --> 00:13:30.075
Like, I laid in

00:13:30.075 --> 00:13:31.743
that if Stevie Nicks
is mad at you,

00:13:31.743 --> 00:13:34.179
she leaves a scarf
on your pillow,

00:13:34.179 --> 00:13:36.215
and I feel like
it didn't get anything.

00:13:39.551 --> 00:13:41.453
And so, like, I've set
something up and I'm like,

00:13:41.453 --> 00:13:43.155
now do I call it back
by revealing

00:13:43.155 --> 00:13:46.191
that I've run a scarf
up my sleeve?

00:13:46.191 --> 00:13:48.194
[ Laughter ]

00:13:50.762 --> 00:13:52.464
Like, does that pay off at all?

00:13:55.801 --> 00:13:58.303
[ Chuckles ]

00:13:58.303 --> 00:14:00.339
I think we're a little rusty.

00:14:00.339 --> 00:14:02.774
[ Laughter ]

00:14:02.774 --> 00:14:05.444
Some people forgot
what time it started.

00:14:05.444 --> 00:14:07.112
[ Laughter ]

00:14:09.114 --> 00:14:10.916
But you know what?

00:14:10.916 --> 00:14:13.919
[Bleep]
I hate to say it.

00:14:13.919 --> 00:14:17.656
Missed you guys.
Missed the jackals.

00:14:17.656 --> 00:14:19.525
Codependency.
I've made a codependency

00:14:19.525 --> 00:14:21.393
with a bunch of [bleep] jackals.

00:14:25.597 --> 00:14:27.433 line:0%
It's great to be back.
And...

00:14:27.433 --> 00:14:29.268 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:14:42.347 --> 00:14:44.750
You know, as I'm --
as I'm watching this

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:46.452
in the monitor...

00:14:49.187 --> 00:14:50.322
...one thing really...

00:14:50.322 --> 00:14:51.656
There's like one thought
I'm having.

00:14:51.656 --> 00:14:53.826
This shouldn't be
Emmy-nominated.

00:14:53.826 --> 00:14:55.761
[ Laughter ]

00:14:55.761 --> 00:14:57.096
See me next week.

